<h1>Results</h1>
This is actual output captured from running `mpirun -n 4 ./mpi-logger`. Because the ranks run concurrently, the exact
interleaving of the per-rank lines varies from run to run; some repeated lines have been collapsed with `...` for
brevity:

@code{.cpp}

Starting distributed solver apply (will trigger MPI events)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
[Rank 1] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 1] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
[Rank 1] AllToAll started...
[Rank 2] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 2] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
[Rank 2] AllToAll started...
[Rank 2] AllToAll completed.
[Rank 3] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 3] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
[Rank 3] AllToAll started...
[Rank 3] AllToAll completed.
[Rank 0] AllToAll started...
[Rank 0] AllToAll completed.
[Rank 1] AllToAll completed.
...
[Rank 0] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
Distributed solver apply completed.
Starting distributed vector dot product (will trigger MPI all_reduce)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
...
Dot product result: 16

@endcode

Each MPI operation issued through the logged communicator produces a matching <code>_started</code> /
<code>_completed</code> pair, tagged with the rank and the element/byte counts.
